# UdhaM — App Features

This file is the product-facing feature inventory for UdhaM. It lists capabilities intended to be available in the app, not implementation details, architecture decisions, or deferred ideas.

## 1. Account and access

- Sign in with Google.
- Use the same account across supported devices.
- View and manage basic profile information.
- Sign out securely.

## 2. Groups and members

- Create and manage multiple expense-sharing groups.
- Join groups through invitations.
- View group members and group activity.
- Add guest participants who do not yet have an UdhaM account.
- Link a guest participant to their account through a controlled process when they join UdhaM.

## 3. Expense management

- Create, view, and edit expense records.
- Record expenses with a description, amount, date, category, and optional notes.
- Record an expected payer separately from the person who actually pays.
- Create an expense even when it has not been paid yet.
- Add one or more participants to an expense.
- Split expenses equally or enter custom share amounts.
- View each participant's exact share.
- Track unpaid, partially paid, paid, and voided expense states.
- View expenses in a date-based group ledger.

## 4. Payments and allocations

- Record actual payments made by group members.
- Record the payer, amount, date, and optional payment reference or note.
- Allocate one payment across multiple expenses.
- Allocate multiple payments to a single expense.
- Support partial payments and show the remaining amount due.
- View which payments covered each expense.
- Keep payments separate from the expenses they cover.

## 5. Balances and settlements

- View each member's balance within a group.
- See how much each member has paid and how much they owe through their expense shares.
- See who owes whom and understand the underlying amounts.
- View suggested settlements separately from completed transfers.
- Record actual settlements between members.
- Keep settlement records separate from ordinary expenses and payments.

## 6. Receipts and payment proof

- Attach receipts or payment proof to an expense or payment.
- View attachments from the relevant record.
- See upload progress and whether an attachment is queued, uploading, uploaded, or failed.
- Retry failed uploads.

## 7. Smart Payment Detection

- Offer an optional Smart Inbox for detected financial transactions.
- On supported Android devices, detect eligible bank and UPI transaction SMS messages where platform permissions and distribution policies allow it.
- Parse eligible messages on-device into transaction candidates, such as debit or credit direction, amount, date, counterparty, and transaction reference when available.
- Let users review, correct, confirm, ignore, or identify duplicate candidates.
- Convert a confirmed candidate into a personal transaction, group expense, payment, or settlement as appropriate.
- Allow a confirmed payment to be allocated across one or more existing expenses.
- Never create a shared expense, payment allocation, or settlement without user confirmation.
- Keep raw SMS message content on the device; do not upload the user's SMS inbox or raw message bodies to UdhaM.
- Provide controls to enable or disable detection and manage pending local candidates.

**Platform availability:** Automatic general-inbox SMS detection is an Android-only capability and depends on device support, permission availability, and applicable app-store policy approval. On iOS, users can enter transactions manually or use explicitly supported user-initiated import options; UdhaM will not claim general SMS inbox access.

## 8. Activity and history

- View a chronological history of expenses, payments, allocations, settlements, and relevant record changes.
- Filter activity by date, member, or transaction type.
- Open a transaction to view its full details and related records.

## 9. Offline access and synchronization

- View previously available group and ledger data while offline.
- Create and update supported records while offline.
- Queue changes and attachments for synchronization.
- Show pending, syncing, synchronized, and failed states.
- Retry failed synchronization.
- Synchronize group data across devices after sign-in.
- Preserve queued financial changes rather than silently discarding them.

## 10. Preferences and account settings

- Manage profile details.
- Configure available app preferences.
- Control Smart Payment Detection where supported.
- View synchronization status.
- Manage notification and theme preferences as supported by the release.

---

## Product behavior guarantees

- An expected payer is never treated as the actual payer unless a real payment is recorded.
- An unpaid expense remains visible as unpaid.
- A payment does not merge or replace the expenses it covers.
- Expense shares must add up exactly to the expense total.
- Payment allocations must be traceable to their payment and expense records.
- Suggested settlements do not change balances until an actual settlement is recorded.
- SMS-detected transactions do not enter the shared ledger until the user confirms them.
- Financial amounts are handled without floating-point rounding errors.
